[00:04.48] The rusted chains of prison moons
[00:10.10] Are shattered by the sun.
[00:10.64] I walk a road, horizons change
[00:10.64] The tournaments begun.
[00:10.64] The purple piper plays his tune,
[00:10.64] The choir softly sing
[00:10.64] Three lullabies in an ancient tongue,
[00:10.64] For the court of the crimson king.
[00:23.18] The keeper of the city keys
[00:25.60] Put shutters on the dreams.
[00:50.40] I wait outside the pilgrims door
[00:53.62] With insufficient schemes.
[00:55.04] The black queen chants
[00:55.42] The funeral march,
[00:56.86] The cracked brass bells will ring;
[01:00.82] To summon back the fire witch
[01:03.98] To the court of the crimson king.
[01:10.76] The gardener plants an evergreen
[01:10.76] Whilst trampling on a flower.
[01:10.76] I chase the wind of a prism ship
[01:10.76] To taste the sweet and sour.
[01:10.76] The pattern juggler lifts his hand
[01:10.76] The orchestra begin.
[01:10.76] As slowly turns the grinding wheel
[01:10.76] In the court of the crimson king.
[01:41.54] On soft gray mornings widows cry
[01:45.74] The wise men share a joke.
[01:45.74] I run to grasp divining signs
[01:48.70] To satisfy the hoax.
[01:53.28] The yellow jester does not play
[01:59.38] But gentle pulls the strings
[02:01.34] And smiles as the puppets dance
[02:04.14] In the court of the crimson king.
